  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 15,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "index": 0,
          "bbox": [
            0.479,
            0.069,
            0.815,
            0.087
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Measuring Space: Perimeter and Area"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.844,
            0.068,
            0.884,
            0.085
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "133"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.108,
            0.886,
            0.185
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Do you see why the two triangles fit together to make a parallelogram? (If you study the angles in the figure "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "( \\mathrm{e.g.,} \\angle \\mathrm{B^{\\prime}C^{\\prime}A^{\\prime}}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and ∠BCA), you will see why this is so. Keep in mind the criterion by which we check whether two lines are parallel.)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.148,
            0.185,
            0.818,
            0.206
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We already know, area of a parallelogram: base × height = bh."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.207,
            0.848,
            0.239
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, the formula for the area a triangle is "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{1}{2} \\left(  base  \\times  height  \\right) = \\frac{1}{2}   bh."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.245,
            0.886,
            0.304
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A property of the median of a triangle",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ". From the above formula we reach a simple but beautiful conclusion about any of the medians of a triangle."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.138,
            0.318,
            0.462,
            0.507
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 6,
              "bbox": [
                0.138,
                0.318,
                0.462,
                0.507
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_15_image_6.jpg",
              "content": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "image_caption",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.261,
                0.517,
                0.339,
                0.535
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "Fig. 6.22"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.483,
            0.317,
            0.88,
            0.397
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A median is the line segment joining a vertex of the triangle to the midpoint of the opposite side. In Fig. 6.22, AD is a median of "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta \\mathrm { A B C }"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.483,
            0.4,
            0.877,
            0.529
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Consider "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta \\mathrm { A B D }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and ΔACD. Their bases are equal "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\mathrm{BD} = \\mathrm{DC}"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " and they have equal height h. Using the formula for the area of a triangle, we see that they have equal area "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\frac{ah}{2} \\leq 9."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " units!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.52,
            0.53,
            0.815,
            0.55
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We state this as a theorem."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.562,
            0.886,
            0.601
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Theorem",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ": A median of a triangle divides it into two triangles with equal area."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.601,
            0.885,
            0.661
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Does this come as a surprise? It should! After all, ΔABD and ΔACD are (in general) differently shaped (i.e., not congruent to each other). But we have just proved that they have the same area!"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.687,
            0.399,
            0.71
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Think and Reflect"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.128,
            0.724,
            0.855,
            0.784
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Since ΔABD and ΔACD have equal area, you may wonder — Can we divide ΔABD using straight cuts into two or more pieces that we can then rearrange to exactly cover "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "\\Delta \\mathrm { A C D ? }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " What do you think? Is it possible?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.808,
            0.886,
            0.868
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We shall spoil the surprise by revealing that it is possible. But we will not tell you the least number of pieces required. Try to find the answer!"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
